<title>GREECE: BEFORE THE BELL: STOCKS TRADE EX-DIV FRIDAY.</title>
<headline>BEFORE THE BELL: STOCKS TRADE EX-DIV FRIDAY.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Athens stock exchange said</p>
<p>shares of Athens Medical , Parnassos ,</p>
<p>Atemke , Bank of Central Greece ,</p>
<p>Nimatemboriki and Athens Medical-Paleo Faliro </p>
<p>will trade ex-dividend on Friday.</p>
<p>Also, shares of Elviemek will be suspended from</p>
<p>trade.</p>
<p>The adjusted starting prices will have as follows:</p>
<p>    Nimatemboriki			5,231   drachmas</p>
<p>    Bank of Attica *		   1,277</p>
<p>    Athens Medical*		    1,990</p>
<p>    Athens Medical-Faliro*	   1,762</p>
<p>    General Bank *		    10,000</p>
<p>    Parnassos				524</p>
<p>    Bank of Central Greece ord     2,730</p>
<p>				   pref    2,536</p>
<p>(*) also trading ex-bonus</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
